  "image": "https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/digimoncardgame/images/d/d4/BT17-031.png/revision/latest?cb=20240720075634",
  "inheritedEffect": "[Your Turn] [Once Per Turn] When you use an Option card with a cost of 2 or more, 1 of your opponent's Digimon gains ＜Security A. -1＞ (This Digimon checks 1 fewer security card.) until the end of their turn.",
  "level": "3",
  "name": "Renamon",
  "nameJapanese": "レナモン",
  "playCost": "3",
  "rarity": "Common",
  "rulings": {
    "references": [
      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT17-031#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT17-031 (Sep. 6, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, even if you only reveal one of the applicable cards, you can still add it to your hand.",
        "question": "If the 3 cards I reveal from my deck for this card's effect include only either a Digimon card with [Kyubimon], [Taomon], or [Sakuyamon] or [Rika Nonaka] or 1 Option card with a cost of 2 or more, can I just add that 1 card to my hand?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No. If you have cards that are targets of this effect, you must add as many cards to your hand as possible.",
        "question": "If the 3 cards I reveal from my deck for this card's effect include both a Digimon card with [Kyubimon], [Taomon], or [Sakuyamon] and [Rika Nonaka] or 1 Option card with a cost of 2 or more, can I choose to only add one of them to my hand, and place the remaining cards at the bottom of my deck?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, as long as the Option card you use has a cost of 2 or more, this card's inherited effect activates regardless of the actual cost paid.",
        "question": "If I activate an effect that reduces the cost of an Option card with a cost of 2 or more and I only pay a cost of 1, or if I do not pay the cost at all by activating an effect that allows me to use an Option card without paying the cost, does this card's inherited effect activate?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, it doesn’t activate.  It doesn't activate if the cost of an Option card consistently changes when it's in the hand and becomes 1 or less due to that card's effect.",
        "question": "Does this card's inherited effect activate if I use an Option card when it has a cost of 1 or less due to a \"reduce the cost of this card in the hand by 1\" effect on a card such as  such as BT2-099 [Glorious Burst] or BT8-097 [Crimson Blaze]?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
